    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.cursorword\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently mini.cursorword seems to define its highlighting in the setup function: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/cursorword.lua#L123-L127\r\n\r\nThis means that the highlighting will be cleared if a colorscheme is loaded afterwards:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7985687/221374082-fe2a0454-1d68-4afa-8f30-609184b0bc04.png)\r\n\r\nMy suggestion would be to go with the common plugin pattern of setting those highlight in a `ColorScheme` autocmd to prevent this problem.\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-02-26T10:21:59Z",
