    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thank you for the issue!\r\n\r\nHmm... This seems to affect all highlight groups which are defined with `hi default ...` and not `hi default link`.\r\n\r\nHowever, using only `ColorScheme` event seems to be not enough: what if color scheme without `MiniCursorword` highlight group definition is loaded *before* 'mini.cursorword'? Then no 'MiniCursorword' highlight group will be created at all.\r\n\r\nI'll think about the best solution.\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, please consider using one of these approaches:\r\n- Load color scheme first. It seems like a good idea anyway: load color scheme before everything else.\r\n- Define manually `MiniCursorword` highlight group in `ColorScheme` event.\r\n- Add 'mini.nvim' integration in the color scheme you are using. The best option, if you'd ask me :)\r\n\r\n(Off-topic edit: those are some crazy, in a good way, dotfiles you've got there. Nice!)",
            "created_at": "2023-02-25T19:08:50Z",
