        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Sorry I should have been clearer, I believe usually the pattern is to define your highlight in a function that you can call initially as usual. However, in addition to that, you have the `ColorScheme` autocmd that ensure that they do not get cleared. \r\n\r\nAt least that seems to be the way that I have seen it done in most popular plugins.\r\nDon't have time to look at a lot of examples, but of the top of my head:\r\nhttps://github.com/folke/noice.nvim/blob/d8a1f3056ad713b5d471048f8d029264828e22c0/lua/noice/config/init.lua#L253-L258\r\nhttps://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/f388995990aba04cfdc7c3ab870c33e280601109/lua/gitsigns.lua#L462",
            "created_at": "2023-02-25T19:24:00Z",
