        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Sorry I should have been clearer, I believe usually the pattern is to define your highlight in a function that you can call initially as usual. However, in addition to that, you have the `ColorScheme` autocmd that ensure that they do not get cleared.\r\n> \r\n> At least that seems to be the way that I have seen it done in most popular plugins. Don't have time to look at a lot of examples, but of the top of my head: https://github.com/folke/noice.nvim/blob/d8a1f3056ad713b5d471048f8d029264828e22c0/lua/noice/config/init.lua#L253-L258 https://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/f388995990aba04cfdc7c3ab870c33e280601109/lua/gitsigns.lua#L462\r\n\r\nSure, sure. It is just not that big of an issue with most modules, because highlight groups are usually defined with `hi default link` which doesn't get cleared. I've just missed the ones which are defined explicitly without linking.",
